Talking points: 
We have taken time to understand our current state architecture: Its limitations and where we need to change:
Proliferation of >4k applications across IT driven by reacting to ad hoc business requirements, building point solutions vs. reusing standard services, and continual integration of acquisitions
Majority of applications are 3rd party but highly customized but there is heavy customization due to complex business requirements, making upgrades complex, less frequent, time-consuming and costly
Extensive on-premises portfolio: Large fraction of the portfolio is not on cloud (>80% apps); with a few pockets of cloud-native applications
Limited horizontal integration and data threading App. proliferation and point-to-point integrations limits the ability to view data consistently & accurately
Limited flexibility to support new business models across the value chain (inflexible back-office, rigid compensation models, fragmented reporting etc.)

In order to drive to our target, we will use a rigorous prioritization of work to ensure it is critical for the business, employs industry best practices, and adheres to our future state IT principles (for example cloud first, portability, vendor agnosticism, No Ops, Self Service, among others)

When we look at our target state – we have high aspirations, we want to drive the transformation across our ecosystem of customers, partners , suppliers, and a few new characteristics are paramount:
Manage a world-class Hybrid multi-cloud environment
Shift toward 3rd-party infra and standard SaaS deployments
Build to differentiate: Buy commodities, but customize where it differentiates us
Design best-in-class employee digital experience & tools
Innovate: esp. with AI, data & analytics, APIs everywhere (especially important to drive transformation across customers, partners and suppliers)
Operate in an Agile + NoOps environment
Strive for data fidelity

To achieve all of these goals, we will transform our operating model: We will engage in new ways of working with the business where we will be more orchestrators than enablers of incremental functionality, we will establish new governance structures (strategy/architecture/portfolio), we will drive our run/change versus transformation functions in differentiated ways,  we will build strategic partnerships.




