Information Architecture

Identification and definition of site content and functionality with a nomenclature that define the relationships between a site's content/functionality.
Sketching
Distinctive form of drawing which designers use to propose, explore, refine and communicate their ideas.
CXResearch
Wireframing
Visual guide that represents the skeletal framework of a website acting as a jumping-off point for the product design process. 
Service Blueprint
Visualizes the relationships between different service components people, props and processes  that are directly tied to touchpoints in a specific customer journey.


CX Mapping

CX Research
38

Build on UX Blueprint

Why Service Blueprint 
Benefits: 
Gives an organization a comprehensive understanding of its service and the underlying resources and processes.
Discover Weaknesses
Blueprinting exposes the big picture and offers a map of dependencies, thus allowing a business to discover a weak leak at its roots.

Scalability and flexibility
Service blueprints accommodate as much or as little detail as needed showing high-level overviews or intricate steps.
Cross-functionality and knowledge transferability
Service blueprints clarify interactions and reduce silos as complex processes can easily lose sight of the bigger picture and how each actions affects other elements.
Competition
It allows you to compare what you want your service to look like with what it looks like now, or you can compare your company’s services with a competitor’s.
Simple development and deployment
The higher-throughput means you can serve more customers from an application given the same hardware, further reducing the need to invest in servers and hosting infrastructure.
