A living product with a roadmap & backlog, serving an ecosystem
Maintaining the Design System

www.intelligaia.com
It was difficult to discover one naming convention that was appropriate across all components. Taking the time to set this convention was an integral part of the process in order to develop a common language. 
Speaking a Common Language
We strived to create the least amount of components that are robust enough to be applied to a large amount of use cases. We foresee this system growing infinitely and have an auditing process in place to maintain the quality of the system, overall. 
Avoid Duplicates by Auditing
Safeguard Content with Version Control
Keeping comprehensive documentation is necessary when implementing a new system. Our current documentation exists in the form of a Figma file link that allows users to browse components with visuals and links from live production code.
Documentation Every Step of the Way
Version History allows us to view, restore or duplicate an older version of our file at any time. Versions are automatically saved when there have been no changes to the file for 30 minutes.

